<section class="chapter" aria-label="Signals">
  <div class="chapter__inner">
    <h2 class="section-title">Signals</h2>
    <p class="muted">Signals are the observable evidence of how work actually happens — turning everyday activity into measurable inputs the system can interpret and act on.</p>
    <p>Every hiring process generates thousands of data points about the process, the people, and decision quality. Individually they look like noise. Collectively, they reveal patterns in workflow health, behavioral dynamics, and decision-making that show where intervention is needed.</p>
    
    <div class="callout"><b>Signals don’t just feed the system. They run the system.</b></div>

    <p>Modern tools make it possible to track not just traditional workflow metrics like pass-through rates, and time-to-fill, but also uncommonly tracked signals that reveal deeper system behavior using methods drawn from decision science, organizational psychology, and behavioral economics.</p>

    <div class="grid3">

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Workflow Signals</h3>
        <p class="muted">How <strong>work moves</strong> in the process.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pass-through rates</li>
          <li>Stage transitions</li>
          <li>Time in stage</li>
          <li>Scheduling delays</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="/tools/metrics/">See Metrics A[i]gent →</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Behavioral Signals</h3>
        <p class="muted">How <strong>people perform</strong>.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Responsiveness</li>
          <li>Communication clarity</li>
          <li>Attention to detail</li>
          <li>Follow-through</li>
        </ul>

      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Decision Signals</h3>
        <p class="muted"><strong>Hiring decisions</strong> reliability.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Decision consistency</li>
          <li>Interviewer scoring variance</li>
          <li>Rubric adherence</li>
          <li>Override frequency</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="/articles/decision-science-metrics/">Related article →</a></p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <p>Signals are not dashboards and they are not opinions. They are structured evidence the system can observe, compare, and act on.</p>

  </div>
</section>

